  "body": "Follow-ups from the review of PR #809 (#789, workholding accessories), stacked on PR #802 (#788, vises): https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/809#pullrequestreview-5856284178\n\n1. **Forward compatibility of the project key (most important):** `FixtureDto`'s `accessory` key is a tagged serde enum. An unknown `kind` or a missing field fails the WHOLE project load (a clean error, not a crash) instead of dropping the key and logging it, as the nonsense-value path does. Once a later release adds a kind, this build refuses those files entirely.\n   - Parse the key leniently: unknown kind or bad shape → drop the key, log it, keep the fixture as plain steel.\n   - Check #802's `vise` key the same way.\n   - Pin both with a file carrying an unknown kind.\n2. **A stud wider than the strap** (`accessory/mesh.rs:146-147`) is allowed, but the band through the strap is drawn only as wide as the strap, narrower than the typed stud figure. Refuse it by name, or add a ring shell.\n3. **The parallels fit sinks the vise** below the table plane when the stock sits on the floor. That's by design, but show a hint in the dialog.\n4. **The parallels \"Height\" field** stays editable in fit mode although the fit overrides it. Disable it, or label it as overridden.\n\nEffort: high (the project file format and fixture geometry).\n\n**Done means:** an unknown accessory or vise kind in a file loads with the key dropped and logged, the stud-width case is refused or modelled, and the two UI hints are in. Each is pinned.\n\nPart of #339.\n",
